/*!
    \title Qt for HarmonyOS Window Drag Key Frame Example
    \example platform/harmonywindowdragkeyframe
    \examplecategory {Mobile}
    \meta tag {widgets,harmonyos,window}

    \brief Sets the key frame policy for resizing the window of a Qt
    application on HarmonyOS.

    While the user resizes a window by dragging its edge, the platform can
    report the new size only at key frames instead of continuously. The key
    frame policy of the window enables this mode and sets when the key
    frames come. The example sets the policy with the
    \c setDragKeyFramePolicy() method of its \c window.Window.

    The policy is collected on the Qt thread as a QJsonObject, with only the
    parameters that are set. The window gets its \c window.Window from
    QNativeInterface::QHarmonyWindow on the Qt thread, as a
    QHarmonyJsObjectRef handle, and hands both to the JS thread:

    \snippet platform/harmonywindowdragkeyframe/main.cpp 0

    On the JS thread, the task maps the policy to a JS object with
    QtHarmony::mapQJsonObjectToJsObject() and calls
    \c setDragKeyFramePolicy(). The promise that it returns resolves to the
    policy that is in effect. The handler maps that policy back with
    QtHarmony::mapJsObjectToQJsonObject() and posts it to the Qt thread
    with QNativeInterface::QHarmonyApplication::runOnQtThread(), where the
    window logs it. A rejection, or an error that the calls throw, is logged
    in the same way:

    \snippet platform/harmonywindowdragkeyframe/main.cpp 1

    \section1 Running the Example

    Select \uicontrol {Key frame mode enabled} and press
    \uicontrol Apply. Then resize the window by dragging its edge and
    compare it with resizing in the default mode. The log shows the policy
    that is in effect. \uicontrol {Reset to defaults} disables the key frame
    mode.

    The example needs a device on which the user can resize the window by
    dragging its edge. On a phone, the main window fills the screen and
    cannot be resized in this way. On a device that does not support the
    key frame mode, the call fails and the window logs the error.
*/
